# Truth audit, 2026-11-08

This receipt separates source evidence, live observations and work that still needs a source. It claims no deployment.

## Method

Read the requested PARA skill explicitly. Its private corpus was absent. Classifications use “Where will this be useful next?” They are Joel/pi-notes adaptations, not quotations from Forte.

`para.json` classifies all 223 SVX notes, including this receipt: 56 Archives, 18 Areas, 145 Resources and four Projects. Each entry has a confidence, reason, missing fields, next action and source pointer. Two ongoing responsibility notes remain at their existing project paths; the scope authorizes archive moves, not a new system-page registration.

The 56 moved notes have `status: archived`, a dated superseded line and a historical-use warning. Historical source studies remain Resources when their dated evidence is reusable. All 16 system pages stay in `.brain/areas/`.

A curl inventory requested 189 public paths. All returned HTTP 200. This covers every existing lore, system and skill detail route, discovery, and selected indexes. Additional requests checked the public law, resource and prompt routes. A 200 is reachability evidence, not proof of every sentence.

Live OpenAPI and a read-only MCP `tools/list` request each returned the same 23 operation names. No signup, email, feedback, operator or infrastructure mutation ran. The live crawl observes the pre-change deployment. Changed sources still need normal owner merge, deployment and readback.

