## needs_source

- **needs-Joel:** `.pi/APPEND_SYSTEM.md:8` still names `defineCapability` and omits RPC. Editing that file requires approval for public publication. It remains unchanged from the audit baseline. `AGENTS.md` and `packages/capability/src/contract.ts` document `defineContract`, `implement` and the current projections.

- HTTP responses cannot establish warehouse delivery, crash-archive completeness, database health, provider deduplication or old-store cleanup. Those remain qualified live checks for the owner. No private storage access or mail sending ran here.
- The dedicated-store declaration is not a migration-completion receipt. That project remains open for owner verification.
- External quotations and dated third-party studies retain their cited sources and dates. This pass did not replay every recording or refresh every external default branch. Current peer refresh belongs to the separate dependency update.
- Five teaching rewrites belong to wiki. The archive URL repair to `lifecycles-are-machines.svx` is path-only. Pending integration audit: review wiki's final text against its pinned sources after those changes are integrated.
- Source-ready is not deployed. After deployment, read back the changed system and skill pages, OpenAPI and both llms files.

## Rules that changed the work

Keep boundary words honest removed blanket durability guarantees. Version content artifacts preserved pinned historical code and dates. Separate writers kept version and generator changes with their assigned writers. Check the actual artifact separated live observations from undeployed source edits. Plain language replaced obsolete names with current files and operations.

## Validation

`pnpm turbo run check test build` passed all 91 tasks, with 18 cache hits. The site suite passed 90 files and 730 tests. Both Brain validators passed all 223 pages. A separate assertion checked every classification, all 56 archive destinations and superseded lines, relative SVX links and the required sections of all 16 system pages.

Generated HTML and Markdown for 11 changed system, lore and skill routes each contain one H1. Rendered interest text includes the split-index and early-erase limits. This receipt is an evidence inventory, not a deployment receipt. Final snapshot and uncached-generation checks are recorded in the completion report.

## PARA moves

`para.json` contains the complete move ledger with note, from, to and reason. Each note also records its next use and review action.

## Review corrections

| Surface | Claim | Verdict | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Archived dependency-refresh note | The schema evidence link resolves after the move. | fixed | Changed the JSON target to `../../data/better-auth-1711.json`. The file exists. |
| Archived launch notes | Internal checkout names explain where the build ran. | cut | Replaced the checkout jargon with “isolated checkout” and removed the assignment name from that description. |
| Seven archived asset task notes | Quoted parent examples are relative to the task. | fixed | The examples describe the assets' frontmatter. Restored `./<step>.svx`; all seven match the actual asset frontmatter and resolve from their assets. |
| Archived vision steer | Public content cites only public evidence. | fixed | Restored the original historical claim, “content cites both”, while keeping the host name redacted. |
| Request budget | The provider receives an idempotency key. | fixed | The adapter serializes `submissionId` in the JSON body without an idempotency header. Provider deduplication on that field is unverified. |

A Markdown-parser check scanned all 223 notes and resolved 113 relative references without a miss. That total includes 30 frontmatter parents and seven asset-parent examples; 99 references are in archives. Seven extensionless page links resolve to existing SVX source pages. The check covers Markdown links, images, definitions, quoted HTML links and actual frontmatter parents. It does not claim to validate external URLs or dynamic expressions.
